# eve.js-mod-esi: configuration template
#
# The launcher's settings form covers the common settings, so most installs do
# not need this file. To use it, copy it to `.env.txt` in this directory and
# uncomment what you need. `.env.txt` survives a launcher update. Plain `.env`
# also works but does not survive one. Never commit either.
#
# Layers, lowest first: defaults, launcher form (settings.json), .env.txt, .env,
# real environment. The highest layer that sets a key wins, per key, and the
# server console reports any key that overrides the form.
#
# Absent and blank differ. Every key below is commented out, so a copy of this
# file changes nothing. `ESI_MOD_ESI_PORT=` and `ESI_MOD_SSO_ISSUER=`, blank but
# uncommented, turn that listener off, and both blank means dormant. For every
# other key, blank means the default.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line. Whole-line `#` comments only: a `#` after a
# value is part of the value. Wrap a value in matching quotes to keep leading or
# trailing spaces.
#
# See docs/deployment.md and docs/open-decisions.md.

# ESI listener

# Port. Absent means 26005 (D1). Blank turns the listener off. 0 is an error
# here; only the launcher form uses 0 for off. 443, 5222, 26000, 26001, 26002,
# 26003, 26400, 40110 and 40111 are errors too: eve.js uses them.
# ESI_MOD_ESI_PORT=

# Listen address. Default 127.0.0.1. Anything else exposes live game data over
# plain HTTP and warns at boot. In a container use 0.0.0.0, or a published port
# answers connection refused, and restrict access with a "127.0.0.1:" prefix on
# the published port.
# ESI_MOD_ESI_BIND_HOST=

# SSO listener (D6)

# Issuer: the `iss` claim of every token and the discovery document's `issuer`.
# Absent means http://localhost:26006. Blank means no SSO port, no discovery
# document and no signed tokens, while ESI keeps serving.
#
# One absolute URL with an explicit scheme, and no trailing slash, path, query or
# fragment (D7), for example ESI_MOD_SSO_ISSUER=http://host.local:26006
#
# Clients must be able to reach it as written. Changing it invalidates every
# token already issued, so every tool has to sign in again. Choose it before the
# first token is signed.
# ESI_MOD_SSO_ISSUER=

# Port the SSO listener binds. Default 26006 (D1). It must differ from the ESI
# port and from the ports eve.js uses (listed above), and should match the port
# in the issuer: a difference warns, since a port mapping can make it legitimate.
# ESI_MOD_SSO_PORT=

# Listen address. Default 127.0.0.1, with the same warning as the ESI one.
# ESI_MOD_SSO_BIND_HOST=

# Allowed clients

# Absolute path to a JSON file of permitted OAuth clients. Blank means no list,
# which is a complete configuration.
#
# Any client_id is accepted. A redirect_uri must be an exact byte-for-byte match
# in this file, or a loopback address literal (127.0.0.0/8 or [::1], any port,
# http or https). So native tools work without the file; it is for browser-based
# tools served from a real address. "localhost" is a name, not loopback, and must
# be listed to be accepted. There are no wildcards on redirect_uris.
#
#   {
#     "clients": [
#       {
#         "client_id": "1a2b3c4d5e6f7g8h9i0j",
#         "redirect_uris": ["http://host.local:8080/sso/callback"],
#         "client_secret": "optional, see below"
#       },
#       {
#         "client_id": "*",
#         "redirect_uris": ["http://host.local:3000/callback"]
#       }
#     ]
#   }
#
# "*" lets any client_id use those URIs, and may not carry a secret.
#
# client_secret is optional. Omitted, the entry is a public client, the normal
# case for a native tool. You invent the secret and configure both this file and
# the tool. Use only A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ - (at least 16 and at most 255 characters);
# `openssl rand -hex 32` qualifies. "~" is excluded because form serializers
# disagree on encoding it. An unusable secret stops the SSO listener at boot.
#
# An authorize request without a PKCE code_challenge is accepted, but its code can
# be redeemed only by a client that authenticated. With no secret configured, such
# a code is unredeemable, and the tool fails at the token exchange.
#
# Keep the file outside this directory. Once an entry has a client_secret it is a
# credential file: keep it out of version control. A path that is set and cannot
# be read is a configuration error and the mod goes inert.
# ESI_MOD_SSO_CLIENTS_PATH=

# Development identity shortcut (D3)

# Skips the in-game bind code and gives every caller a token for the character
# below, for automated tests. Off unless set to 1, true, yes or on. Anyone who can
# reach the SSO port gets that character's data, so it warns whenever it is on,
# and it is a configuration error unless ESI_MOD_SSO_BIND_HOST is loopback.
# ESI_MOD_DEV_AUTO_APPROVE=

# The character auto-approve issues tokens for. Required when auto-approve is on,
# ignored with a warning when it is off.
# ESI_MOD_DEV_AUTO_APPROVE_CHARACTER_ID=

# SSO state

# Override for the directory holding the durable secrets. Blank is normal: the
# default is <game store root>/../sso/, beside the game's sde/ and market/.
#
#   signing-key.pem       signs every access token (D8)
#   owner-salt.txt        makes the `owner` claim opaque
#   refresh-tokens.jsonl  grants that outlive a restart (D30)
#
# Back up all three together. Losing the key invalidates issued access tokens.
# Losing the salt moves every character's `owner` claim, which clients read as a
# character transfer. Losing the store logs every tool out. A damaged file is never
# regenerated: the SSO listener refuses to start, names the file, and waits for a
# deliberate `mv`.
#
# Set this when there is no game store to derive from, or for a volume chosen to
# outlive it. It must be absolute, because a relative path depends on which process
# resolves it. Pointing it inside this directory is an error, because a redeploy
# replaces this directory (D21). If you use a plain `.env` for this, losing that file
# on a launcher update creates new credentials; use `.env.txt`.
# ESI_MOD_SSO_STATE_DIR=

# Token signing

# Override for the key file alone, for a key you supply. Blank is normal. PKCS#8
# from `openssl genpkey` works directly (D8). To move all three files, use
# ESI_MOD_SSO_STATE_DIR instead; if you set both, back up the key's location as well.
# Must be absolute. Keep it outside this directory; pointing inside warns, because a
# redeploy would destroy the key and invalidate every issued token.
# ESI_MOD_SIGNING_KEY_PATH=

# Error budget (D44)

# Errors a caller may spend in 60 seconds before this replica answers 420. A whole
# number, at least 1. Default 100, CCP's observed budget, which matches Tranquility.
# Raising it is a deliberate divergence, for a client that asks about many unknown
# characters at startup and empties the budget on honest 404s.
# ESI_MOD_ERROR_LIMIT_MAX_ERRORS=

# Logging

# One of error, warn, info, debug. Default info. Shares stdout with the game server,
# so debug is noisy. An unrecognised level warns and uses the default.
# ESI_MOD_LOG_LEVEL=
